Package: shure-mv7
Version: @VERSION@-1
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Annika Wickert <awlx@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: udev, xdg-utils
Recommends: gjs, gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.10), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.4), gir1.2-soup-3.0, pulseaudio-utils
Suggests: gnome-shell (>= 45)
Homepage: https://github.com/awlx/mv7-linux-support
Description: Unofficial Linux web console for the Shure MV7+ microphone
 This independent application controls a Shure MV7+ microphone through its
 vendor HID interface and serves an embedded local web interface for gain,
 DSP, monitoring, reverb, LED, and mute controls. It is not affiliated with,
 endorsed by, or supported by Shure Incorporated.
 Includes a native GTK4/libadwaita application and GNOME Shell panel controls
 backed by the same local daemon.